<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli uses your camera to scan barcodes, scan receipts, and identify fresh ingredients with Freshli Vision. If you enable the optional Gaze-Adaptive UI accessibility feature in Settings, Freshli also uses the TrueDepth camera via ARKit face tracking purely on-device to compute where you are looking on screen — no face data is ever stored, transmitted, or shared.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli accesses your photos to add images to pantry items and community listings.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli saves shared recipe images and impact cards to your photo library.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli uses your location to show nearby community food listings and set pickup locations.</string>
	<key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
	<false/>
